Your task is to append a postscript to the main instruction for this task: {{ instance.task }}

The main instruction is fixed:
<instruction>{{ main_prompt }}</instruction>

Optimize these metrics jointly: {{ metrics | tojson }}. Higher metric values are better.
Scores below are negative mean ranks across the metrics over all training candidates.
Higher scores are better; they are recomputed as new candidates enter the archive.
Below are previous postscripts with their scores and critiques, ordered from lower to higher score.
{% for item in trajectory %}
<rated_postscript>
<postscript>{{ item.text }}</postscript>
<score>{{ item.score }}</score>
<metrics>{{ item.metrics | tojson }}</metrics>
<critique>{{ item.critique }}</critique>
</rated_postscript>
{% endfor %}

Generate a short postscript that is different from the postscripts above and aims for a higher score.
It should be concise, effective, and generally applicable to unseen inputs.

1. Compare high-score postscripts to low-score ones and synthesize their critiques and suggestions. List concise actionable improvements in <suggestion> tags.
2. Apply the suggestions to improve the additional metrics while preserving performance on {{ instance.primary_metric }}.
3. Vary wording, paraphrase, phrase order, grammar, and sentence order.
4. Write only the final new postscript in one nonempty <postscript>...</postscript> block.

Do not rewrite or repeat the main instruction. Do not introduce data placeholders or copy reference answers.
